Description: Tools for compositional data analysis (CoDA) of time-use behaviour,
    such as the 24-hour composition of sleep, sedentary behaviour, light
    physical activity and moderate-to-vigorous physical activity. A composition
    is declared once and then modelled as a predictor of an outcome. It enters
    each model through its isometric log-ratio (ILR) coordinates, computed with
    'robCompositions'. The models include linear, generalized linear, Cox
    proportional hazards, ordinal, multinomial and robust linear models, with
    multilevel (mixed) variants. The package estimates the effect of
    reallocating time between behaviours (compositional isotemporal
    substitution) and plots compositions and reallocations. Predictions and
    reallocation contrasts, with their confidence intervals, come from
    'emmeans'.
